<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWrecks.xml                    UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S6 "burning-shallows wreck salvage"
  (scald_kit_spec.md §S6: "RUT_ScaldWreck* building defs (2-3 silhouettes,
  art pass) scattered at map-gen in shallow scald water ... Salvage is
  vanilla deconstruct/smash yields").

  ===========================================================================
  CRIB TARGET — Core's own ShipChunkBase, read in full this pass
  ===========================================================================
  Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_Exotic.xml:130-180,
  ParentName="BuildingBase" Name="ShipChunkBase" (defName ShipChunk): a
  static, non-buildable (no designationCategory), non-claimable, always-
  deconstructible salvage building — deconstruct for costList-derived
  resources, no comps beyond a flavor inspect string, no pawn spawner, no
  rot, no corpse. That is exactly S6's own "cooked clean: no rot, no
  corpses, no hostiles" requirement, structurally, not by a linter rule
  added after the fact. Three defs below crib this shape directly
  (ParentName="ShipChunkBase" — same abstract vanilla already ships, no new
  RM_/RUT_ abstract needed) rather than JawaGroundHulk's own PrefabDef
  route, which is a hand-placed one-off stamp keyed to a specific ship
  export, not a repeatable map-gen scatter candidate.

  🔴 THREE SILHOUETTES, NOT THREE MECHANICS. Per the spec's own "(2-3
  silhouettes, art pass)" — distinct shapes for scatter variety, all
  carrying the identical salvage mechanism (deconstruct-only, vanilla
  costList/killedLeavings). No new comp, no loot ThingSetMaker: the spec's
  own §S6 text flags "a small RUT_ScaldSalvage loot ThingSetMaker" with a
  ❓ (an open idea, never resolved) alongside the RESOLVED claim that S6
  needs "zero new C#" for the scatter mechanism itself — a ThingSetMaker
  wired to fire extra loot ON deconstruct would need a comp to hook
  Notify_Deconstructed or similar, which is new C# the spec's own build-
  order item never asked for at S6's "S" effort rating. Deferred to the
  loot pass (scald_kit_spec.md §S6: "Loot REGISTER ... is the items pass's,
  per sheet economy convention") rather than invented here. v1 ships the
  vanilla costList/killedLeavings salvage only, same mechanism ShipChunk
  itself already uses.

  Values below are INVENTED, stated plainly: sized down from
  ShipChunk_Mech's 40 Steel/15 GravlitePanel (a fresh mechanoid chunk) since
  these have sat cooking in near-boiling water — corrosion costs some of
  the yield back. No uranium/component on any of the three: this is hull
  and tankage, not the caskets JawaGroundHulk already owns.

  ⚠️ Ban 6 (no vanilla-Earth flora/fauna) and Ban 2 (no burn-immunity def)
  both hold structurally: nothing here grants terrain immunity or spawns
  life. The burn-per-tick cost of standing in the shallows to deconstruct
  these is paid by the terrain itself (RUT_ScaldWaterShallow's own
  burnDamage/burnIntervalTicks), never waived — S6's own "the price is
  posted in burns per trip" line is the shipped terrain, unchanged.

  🔴 TERRAIN AFFORDANCE — verified by direct read, not assumed.
  BuildingBase's own default terrainAffordanceNeeded is Light (Core
  Buildings_Base.xml:11). WaterShallowBase's affordance list (Core
  Terrain_Water.xml:103-112) is ShallowWater/WaterproofConduitable/
  Bridgeable/Walkable — no Light. Left at the inherited default, none of
  these three defs could ever pass a placement/scatter affordance check on
  the very terrain they are meant to scatter onto. All three explicitly
  override terrainAffordanceNeeded to Walkable below, the one affordance
  every RUT_ScaldWater*Shallow terrain actually carries.

  Art: one Graphic_Random variant each (_A), artpipe jobs scald_wreck{hull,tank,frame}_v1.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ShipChunkBase">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckHull</defName>
    <label>scalded hull section</label>
    <description>A broken length of hull plate, cooked in the shallows until the paint is gone and the seams have given. What the pan swallowed and gave back. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckHull</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Walkable</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>0.75</resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <Steel>30</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <ChunkSlagSteel>2</ChunkSlagSteel>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ShipChunkBase">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckTank</defName>
    <label>scalded tank wreck</label>
    <description>A ruptured pressure tank, half sunk and scoured smooth by the boil. Whatever it once held is long gone; the shell is still worth the walk. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckTank</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Walkable</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>0.75</resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <Steel>20</Steel>
      <GravlitePanel>5</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <ChunkSlagSteel>1</ChunkSlagSteel>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ShipChunkBase">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckFrame</defName>
    <label>scalded frame wreck</label>
    <description>A stripped strut and frame section, all its skin burned or boiled away, standing bare in the shallows like a rib cage. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckFrame</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Walkable</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>0.75</resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <Steel>15</Steel>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <ChunkSlagSteel>1</ChunkSlagSteel>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
